    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-24T04:10:36+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T04:10:36+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T17:40:36Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T17:40:36Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure that lies near the NT/WA border will combine with a trough and cold front further south to move over much of SA on Saturday, and over the far northeast on Sunday. A ridge of high pressure will then move into the west from late Sunday and persist over the rest of the state throughout next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers near the coast, high chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds and large hail south of Hawker. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the middle of the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of rain, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and early afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of morning frost on and east of the ranges. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending west to southwesterly during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 2 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast, near zero chance elsewhere. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the day then tending south to southwesterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
